- `tasks/velvet-ember/` — hardened `canonical_header` (rejects CR/LF/NUL and all non-RFC-7230-token chars via `HeaderError(ValueError)`) while preserving exact canonical title forms (`etag`→`Etag`, `a--b`→`A--B`, `x501`→`X501`, digits/empty tokens), a WSGI relay (`/app/gateway.py`) with structured `invalid_header`/`duplicate_header`/`bad_request` 400s, and a CLI deliverable `/app/canonical_map.json`
- Hidden cases: a 40-entry normalization matrix (control chars, unicode, spaces, non-strings vs benign token families) exercised both at function level and through the CLI on hidden inputs, plus a 13-step gateway sequence including canonical-collision detection. Explicitly guards against the over-broad-validation failure mode.
